##! `live` (10, "Debugging and profiling"; N-35, D-068): where a running
##! program adopts the newest epoch of hot replacement under `sisu run
##! --watch`. Ambient, as `task` and `log` are.

## A boundary: under `sisu run --watch` the running task adopts the newest
## epoch here, and resolves every call after it in that epoch until its
## next boundary, so one iteration of a loop never mixes an old body with
## a new one. Without `--watch` it does nothing. `Ticker.wait` calls it.
##
## ```
## for _ in range(3):
##     live.boundary()
## ```
@intrinsic("live.boundary")
def boundary()

## The epoch the running task has adopted: 0 until the first swap.
@intrinsic("live.epoch")
def epoch() -> int
